      "prompt": "Explain why bread dough rises to a curious teenager.",
      "reference_response": "Hey there! So, you're wondering why bread dough rises? It's actually pretty cool! When you make bread, you add yeast to the dough. Yeast is a tiny living thing that eats sugar and produces carbon dioxide gas as a byproduct. This gas gets trapped in the dough, causing it to expand and rise. It's like the dough is breathing and getting bigger and bigger! That's why your bread dough rises. Pretty neat, right?\n",
